Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- DEFAULT_REVIEWER_ROLE -> Role.ARCHITECT_CRITIC (the persistent source of truth:
  no registry key / launch env sets the reviewer; ORCHESTRATOR_REVIEWER_ROLE is an
  override). The answer verdict (chat_review) and review_before_commit (chat.py) now
  resolve through resolve_reviewer_role() instead of the literal architect_general;
  the review_before_commit interaction skill moves to architect_critic; the
  PLAN_REVIEWED event records the resolved reviewer.
- New DEFAULT_PLANNER_ROLE = Role.ARCHITECT_CRITIC + resolve_planner_role()
  (override > ORCHESTRATOR_PLANNER_ROLE > default): proactive_stage's decomposition,
  its repair turn and the lineage fallback use it instead of the literal.
- Escalation (graph ArchitectNode, _ESCALATION_MAP, risk_abstain_target_role) still
  targets architect_general (Flash-Next).
- Tests updated; new binding tests in tests/unit/test_roles.py.

